WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:06.150
We've got a pretty good idea which movies
will break the bank at the box office in 2017,

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:11.329
but there's more to the year in movies than
picking blockbusters and super-franchises.

00:00:11.329 --> 00:00:15.389
We've gone over the release schedule, taken
a look at the prevailing trends, and come

00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:20.740
up with some theories about what's happening
at the cineplex over the next 12 months — and

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:21.740
beyond.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.740
Rey's DNA

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:28.500
There are some bets that seem safer than others
when it comes to Star Wars: Episode VIII.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.390
While it's almost a guarantee that there'll
be at least one of these lines thrown into

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:33.030
the script...

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.790
"I gotta bad feeling about this."

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:40.520
...it's less clear which, if any, more throwback
character cameos will come into the mix — or

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:46.370
if any of those parentage issues left lingering
around the new kids on the galactic block

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:47.840
will finally be revealed.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.460
With that in mind, we're predicting Star Wars
fans will learn more about Rey's lineage.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:01:00.000
We expect to see her training with Luke, who
seems at least somewhat likely to be her father

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.439
— and don't forget, Luke found out who his
dad was in the second installment of the original

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:08.200
trilogy, so that would be good timing.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.290
Logan 2.0

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:16.560
Sorry, Wolverine fanatics, but we're predicting
Logan — at least, as portrayed by Hugh Jackman

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.020
— is not long for this world.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:24.030
Not only has his healing ability been compromised
by the hand of time in Logan, but the movie's

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:30.240
trailer also seem to suggest the story will
serve as a full-length introduction for his

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:31.240
replacement.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:36.409
Marvel Comics' Laura Kinney, a.k.a. X-23,
is Logan's cloned daughter in the comics — and

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:39.780
she ultimately assumes his mantle after his
death.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:44.110
Logan seems to be on a suicide mission to
protect her in the trailer — and she's so

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:48.560
cute with those sunglasses, after all — so
we wouldn't be surprised to see him make the

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:53.670
ultimate sacrifice while X-23 comes into play
for The New Mutants.

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:57.020
Especially since that's exactly what happened
in the comics.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.939
Stephen King is king

00:01:58.939 --> 00:02:05.630
Of all modern American authors, perhaps none
has had quite as much of an impact on Hollywood

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:06.700
as Stephen King.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:12.670
His stories have spawned dozens of movie adaptations,
some of which he's liked enough to make cameos

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:13.670
in.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:20.010
His library has also spawned several TV shows
and miniseries, but until now, some of his

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.620
most high-concept stories have remained firmly
shelved.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:28.720
That changes with The Dark Tower, which many
King fans consider the backbone of the author's

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.250
extended story universe.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:35.489
If its big-screen adaptation does well enough
upon arrival later this year, there's definitely

00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:37.840
room for growth in the series.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.410
So prepare for a full-on franchise if the
box office take is right.

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:48.930
And if the upcoming adaptation of King's IT
lands too, you can really get ready to see

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:54.129
filmmakers dive into the King archives for
even more bestsellers that could be turned

00:02:54.129 --> 00:02:56.910
into potential franchises.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.319
Sequel setbacks

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:03.910
Go ahead and free up your calendar space on
June 9th now, because there's just no way

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:08.300
World War Z 2 is going to be in theaters that
day as scheduled.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:13.160
Even several months out, the film still hadn't
even secured a director, and it's not the

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:16.440
only delay that's virtually inevitable this
year.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:22.129
James Cameron's Avatar 2 release date for
2018 will probably get another nudge back

00:03:22.129 --> 00:03:27.599
into 2019, if not further, given the lack
of progress on the production front so far.

00:03:27.599 --> 00:03:35.080
Well, that and the fact that Cameron wants
to make his four Avatar sequels all at once.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:40.460
Meanwhile, don't be surprised if the Jumanji
reboot-slash-sequel gets kicked back again,

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:45.550
too, because it's notoriously had trouble
finding footing — and it wouldn't necessarily

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:51.379
be shocking if Andy Serkis' Jungle Book: Origins
ends up delayed or even scrapped altogether

00:03:51.379 --> 00:03:57.080
in the wake of Disney's critical and commercial
success with its own live-action Jungle Book.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:00.980
"Relax, kid, no need to get worked up, k?"

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:02.159
Galactic expansion

00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:07.950
If we've learned anything from the Disney's
Pixar and Marvel mergers, it's that when Disney

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:13.810
gets its white-gloved paws into something
lucrative, the studio's going to take full

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.190
and eager advantage.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:19.719
"One million, two million, three million,
four!"

00:04:19.719 --> 00:04:24.490
That's already the case with Disney-Lucasfilm,
which will undoubtedly start rolling out more

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:30.099
Star Wars sequels, prequels, and standalone
stories now that Rogue One has confirmed that

00:04:30.099 --> 00:04:35.009
the franchise is viable even outside of the
Luke-Leia-Han Solo story axis.

00:04:35.009 --> 00:04:40.740
With the Han Solo prequel on deck for 2018
and Episode 9 scheduled to follow along in

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:45.830
the summer of 2019, we can probably count
on the Star Wars franchise to start looking

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:51.449
more like the MCU, with two-a-year announcements
trickling in for the release schedule.

00:04:51.449 --> 00:04:55.720
How that impacts the brand's quality, of course,
remains to be seen.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.020
Fingers crossed.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:58.639
Go Gamora

00:04:58.639 --> 00:05:04.099
Since the superhero world seems ever geared
towards expanding its franchise horizons,

00:05:04.099 --> 00:05:10.460
Harley Quinn, Wonder Woman, and Captain Marvel
are all preparing for time in the spotlight.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:15.999
But there's another character who might be
due for some solo screen time: Gamora from

00:05:15.999 --> 00:05:17.379
Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:05:17.379 --> 00:05:23.089
Once Volume 2 drops in May, its inevitably
impressive receipts will probably justify

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:29.060
giving some member of the team his or her
own day in the sun, MCU-style.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:33.279
One could easily argue that Gamora's the ideal
candidate for the job.

00:05:33.279 --> 00:05:38.490
Consider her meaty family story with Thanos
and Nebula, her radness outside of being the

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:42.710
object of Star-Lord's affection — not to
mention the fact that she's currently starring

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.529
in her own solo comics title.

00:05:44.529 --> 00:05:49.649
Gamora will no doubt prove to be key in the
Avengers' fight with Thanos, and if she were

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:55.619
to get a standalone story, it'd mean she could
introduce the badass all-girl warrior group

00:05:55.619 --> 00:05:56.619
the Graces.

00:05:56.619 --> 00:06:02.469
Her credentials are there, and Zoe Saldana
has a proven record at the box office.

00:06:02.469 --> 00:06:04.020
Musicals are in (again)

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:11.259
For all its faults, 2016 did help to usher
in a new generation of movie musicals.

00:06:11.259 --> 00:06:16.449
After successful broadcasts for Grease: Live
and Hairspray Live drummed up impressive ratings

00:06:16.449 --> 00:06:21.271
on the small screen, La La Land reminded everyone
that there's still a place for this type of

00:06:21.271 --> 00:06:23.699
good old-fashioned entertainment in theaters.

00:06:23.699 --> 00:06:29.360
The passing of Singin' in the Rain star Debbie
Reynolds may spark a revival of interest in

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:35.259
classic singalong cinema, or even inspire
a studio or two to take a stab at a remake.

00:06:35.259 --> 00:06:41.929
And Mary Poppins Returns with Emily Blunt
and Lin-Manuel Miranda should get a boost

00:06:41.929 --> 00:06:44.580
thanks to the La La Land appreciation craze.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:50.330
Hollywood stars, take note: it might be wise
to schedule some singing lessons.

00:06:50.330 --> 00:06:51.719
The new kids

00:06:51.719 --> 00:06:57.529
Emma Stone will probably be the awards season
sweetheart of 2017, which means someone might

00:06:57.529 --> 00:07:02.429
finally get the bright idea to put her and
Jennifer Lawrence together in a raunchy buddy

00:07:02.429 --> 00:07:03.689
comedy this year.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:09.330
Now, that pipe dream aside, there will be
plenty of major breakouts in the months to

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:10.330
come.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:14.659
Daniel Kaluuya, for example, is bound for
the big time once his twisty thriller Get

00:07:14.659 --> 00:07:20.220
Out drops and details start to emerge regarding
his part in Marvel's Black Panther.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:23.659
Count on him to capitalize on rising interest
in his talent.

00:07:23.659 --> 00:07:28.229
Alden Ehrenreich, likewise, is a name that
might reach household status this year thanks

00:07:28.229 --> 00:07:32.129
to his forthcoming turn as Han Solo in the
Star Wars spinoff.

00:07:32.129 --> 00:07:38.009
Ehrenreich has an impressive filmography under
his belt already with some small but memorable

00:07:38.009 --> 00:07:41.659
roles, but headlining as Han is a career-maker.

00:07:41.659 --> 00:07:47.800
Meanwhile, actress Sofia Boutella is also
poised to have a major moment this year, after

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:52.759
her work in the reboot of The Mummy and The
Coldest City arrives in theaters.

00:07:52.759 --> 00:07:57.620
The latter project in particular seems promising,
as it's a Cold War spy thriller that gives

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:01.479
her a chance to steal scenes from some of
the industry's elite.

00:08:01.479 --> 00:08:03.629
Just like she did in Star Trek Beyond.

00:08:03.629 --> 00:08:04.789
"Pardon me."

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:06.919
"He likes that seat."

00:08:07.099 --> 00:08:08.110
R.I.P. whitewashing

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:13.739
Unfortunately, this year will bring us multiple
films which will, again, highlight the need

00:08:13.739 --> 00:08:20.029
for studios to stop whitewashing movie casts
— including The Great Wall and Ghost in

00:08:20.029 --> 00:08:24.749
the Shell, both of which have already attracted
their share of controversy.

00:08:24.749 --> 00:08:29.389
Marvel's Doctor Strange somehow managed to
survive its own issues on that front, at least

00:08:29.389 --> 00:08:31.550
where the box office was concerned.

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:36.810
But with these new pictures in particular,
any enthusiasm seems likely to be dampened

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:38.310
by casting backlash.

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:43.589
Perhaps the conversations that result, whether
the films are ultimately successful or not,

00:08:43.589 --> 00:08:48.649
will finally put an end to Hollywood's unfortunate
whitewashing tradition once and for all.

00:08:48.649 --> 00:08:49.649
Fingers crossed.

00:08:49.649 --> 00:08:50.649
Thanks for watching!

00:08:50.649 --> 00:08:53.579
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:53.579 --> 00:08:56.670
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

